properties.description:
Six real-binary tests pinning the class, each a surface a held lock used to leave degraded forever:
- over HTTP, the same process and port serve the design after the holder stops, and /readyz goes 503 → 200;
- a server served for others (--http-allow-host naming another machine) that waited out the lock serves the design under the caller rule a healthy start installs (#616 fix 4): the handshake says SERVED FOR OTHERS and a settle is refused naming --http-trusted-gateway;
- over stdio, the client is told notifications/tools/list_changed and then sees the full list;
- a --shared session whose election timed out re-elects and serves in place;
- /readyz and /healthz answer any Host while the design itself stays gated, and a registry is ready when it is up;
- a stamp that will not read is not polled, and readiness stays 503.
The original five failed against unfixed main (329a074); the caller-rule test failed against the merge of main into this branch before chg:a-design-served-after-a-held-lock-frees-is-prepared-the-way-a-healthy-start-prepares-it.
